   "alt": "The sanctuary of the village church on a Saturday afternoon, getting ready for First Communion. On the left an altar server kneels among spilled blue hymnbooks, the gray-haired sacristan holds up a round white wafer beside a gold plate of wafers, a girl in a white Communion dress and veil twirls, and Père Antoine rehearses from his notes. In the middle a bellhop in red pushes a brass luggage cart of white lilies to the stone altar; behind it a woman dusts the gilded tabernacle. On the right a girl server polishes a gold chalice, a boy holds the tall processional cross and a young woman reads at the lectern from a big book. A rose window and blue lily banners hang above. The open door on the left goes back to the Lady Chapel, the stone steps at the front lead down to the crypt, and the arch on the right opens onto the side aisle with the confessional.",
